  "title": "chore(geometry): delete 62 unreferenced DXF files found by the catalog census",
  "intent": "Owner ruling 2026-09-15, after a census of every DXF under instrument_geometry/: delete the files that nothing reads. 59 cuatro reference traces (two vectorizer runs over the same two plans) and 3 vectorizer page dumps (whole blueprint sheets, not body outlines). The census, its method and its findings are recorded in docs/investigations/dxf_catalog_census_2026-09-15.md. The five files whose measured size disagrees with body/catalog.json are deliberately NOT touched: they are wired into the catalog and specs, and the owner ruled that a separate decision.",
  "change_type": "chore",
  "behavior_change": "No runtime behaviour changes: every deleted file is referenced by no code and no data (verified with git grep over code and data, excluding docs and the archaeology reports). The three cuatro traces that tests read are kept. CI gates: both DXF catalog gates go from 95 files / 65 PASS / 30 QUARANTINED / 0 FAIL to 33 / 6 / 27 / 0, exit 0. The three quarantine records for the deleted page dumps are removed in the same commit, because a record naming a missing asset fails both gates by design.",
